    "message": "Defuse both forms of command a child's report can carry

The report lands on a live parent whose gate is about to wake its agent, so
two lines in the child's own words can cancel the aggregation the report
exists to inform:

- `commandLinesIn` matches `/name` AND `<!-- atomaton:dispatch=name -->` (the
  latter through `DISPATCH_RE`, and it has no `/` in it), so escaping by
  replacing a literal `/` left the marker intact: the thread reader saw an
  ask nobody claimed, and the gate answered `parent-busy` and took its marker
  back. The escape now goes in front of the character the reader starts at,
  found by searching for the first `<` or `/` so that a list bullet keeps its
  place.
- `atomaton:aggregated=N` quoted in the child's report reached the gate's
  idempotency read, which answered `already-aggregated`: no dispatch, no
  marker, no retry. The child's text now goes through `withoutTags` before it
  is folded in, the same reason `fetch_events` runs it on what an agent reads.
  The body's own `llm-context` line is added afterwards and survives.

Tests cover both, including the hand-retyped `dispatch = name` spelling the
tag stripper cannot see and the escape therefore has to cover alone.

Full suite: 2041 pass, 0 fail. Typecheck clean.",
